      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-309947",
      ":question/problem": "A curve is defined by $y = f(x)$, where $f(x) = 2x^{2} - 3x + 4$. If $y = g(x)$ is a horizontal translation of $y = f(x)$ by $3$ units right, what is the function $g(x)$?"
